  "full_text": "15 August 2024 GACL News GACL Celebrates 78th Independence Day with Pride and Patriotism Gujarat Alkalies and Chemicals Limited (GACL), a leading Chlor-Alkali corporation, proudly celebrated its 78th Independence Day with great pride and patriotism. The ceremonies took place simultaneously at our Vadodara and Dahej complexes, marking a day of reflection and commitment to our nation’s progress. The celebration commenced with the hoisting of the national flag by Shri Swaroop P. IAS, Managing Director of GACL. The event was attended by senior executives, a large number of employees, and their families, reflecting the unity that characterize our organization. In his address to the gathering, Shri Swaroop P. IAS highlighted the profound significance of the day. He remarked, “Today, we commemorate the strong spirit of our freedom fighters and celebrate the values of progress, unity, and diversity that define our great nation. India’s transformation from a colonized land to a modern powerhouse is nothing short of extraordinary. From our humble beginnings, we have risen to become a source of hope and innovation. Our advancements in education, technology, and industry are a proof of our nation’s collective effort and ambition.” Shri Swaroop P. IAS also shared exciting updates about GACL’s ambitious growth plans, emphasizing that several significant projects are making excellent progress. These initiatives reflect GACL’s ongoing commitment to contributing to the nation’s development and innovation. As part of the celebration, he distributed the Award for Best Suggestion 2023-24 to outstanding employees. This award underscores GACL’s commitment to empowering innovation and recognizing excellence within the organization. Concluding his speech, he extended his heartfelt Independence Day greetings to all present, reinforcing the company’s dedication to fostering a culture of pride and progress."
}